Note: GLSL ES 100 mat3 constructor from columns: mat3(vec3 c0, c1, c2) or 9 floats in column-major order. rotY: columns (cos,0,-sin),(0,1,0),(sin,0,cos). Written as mat3(c,0.0,-s, 0.0,1.0,0.0, s,0.0,c) — that's column-major: col0=(c,0,-s), col1=(0,1,0), col2=(s,0,c). Correct for a Y rotation.

