The box is long; simplify to: `return length(max(abs(p) - b, 0.0)) + min(max(q.x, max(q.y, q.z)), 0.0);` needs q. Write it in full:
```
<span class="t">float</span> <span class="f">sdBox</span>(<span class="t">vec3</span> p, <span class="t">vec3</span> b) {
    <span class="t">vec3</span> q = <span class="f">abs</span>(p) - b;
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="f">length</span>(<span class="f">max</span>(q, <span class="n">0.0</span>)) + <span class="f">min</span>(<span class="f">max</span>(q.x, <span class="f">max</span>(q.y, q.z)), <span class="n">0.0</span>);
}

<span class="c">// Boolean composition — this is how you model with math</span>
<span class="t">float</span> <span class="f">unionSDF</span>(<span class="t">float</span> a, <span class="t">float</span> b)       { <span class="k">return</span> <span class="f">min</span>(a, b); }
<span class="t">float</span> <span class="f">intersectSDF</span>(<span class="t">float</span> a, <span class="t">float</span> b) { <span class="k">return</span> <span class="f">max</span>(a, b); }

<span class="c">// Smooth union — the operator behind metaballs</span>
<span class="t">float</span> <span class="f">smin</span>(<span class="t">float</span> a, <span class="t">float</span> b, <span class="t">float</span> k) {
    <span class="t">float</span> h = <span class="f">clamp</span>(<span class="n">0.5</span> + <span class="n">0.5</span> * (b - a) / k, <span class="n">0.0</span>, <span class="n">1.0</span>);
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="f">mix</span>(b, a, h) - k * h * (<span class="n">1.0</span> - h);
}
```

Sample C "normals_lighting.glsl":
```
<span class="c">// No stored normals: estimate them from the SDF with a tetrahedron</span>
<span class="t">vec3</span> <span class="f">calcNormal</span>(<span class="t">vec3</span> p) {
    <span class="k">const</span> <span class="t">vec2</span> e = <span class="t">vec2</span>(<span class="n">0.001</span>, <span class="n">0.0</span>);
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="f">normalize</span>(<span class="t">vec3</span>(
        <span class="f">sd</span>(p + e.xyy) - <span class="f">sd</span>(p - e.xyy),
        <span class="f">sd</span>(p + e.yxy) - <span class="f">sd</span>(p - e.yxy),
        <span class="f">sd</span>(p + e.yyx) - <span class="f">sd</span>(p - e.yyx)));
}

<span class="t">vec3</span> <span class="f">shade</span>(<span class="t">vec3</span> p, <span class="t">vec3</span> n, <span class="t">vec3</span> rd) {
    <span class="t">vec3</span>  lig = <span class="f">normalize</span>(<span class="t">vec3</span>(<span class="n">0.7</span>, <span class="n">0.9</span>, -<span class="n">0.4</span>));
    <span class="t">float</span> dif = <span class="f">clamp</span>(<span class="f">dot</span>(n, lig), <span class="n">0.0</span>, <span class="n">1.0</span>);
    <span class="t">float</span> bac = <span class="f">clamp</span>(<span class="f">dot</span>(n, -lig), <span class="n">0.0</span>, <span class="n">1.0</span>);
    <span class="t">float</span> fre = <span class="f">pow</span>(<span class="f">clamp</span>(<span class="n">1.0</span> + <span class="f">dot</span>(n, rd), <span class="n">0.0</span>, <span class="n">1.0</span>), <span class="n">3.0</span>);
    <span class="t">vec3</span>  alb = <span class="t">vec3</span>(<span class="n">0.9</span>, <span class="n">0.45</span>, <span class="n">0.3</span>);

    <span class="k">return</span> alb * (<span class="n">0.6</span> * dif + <span class="n">0.25</span> * bac + <span class="n">0.35</span>)      <span class="c">// diffuse · bounce · ambient</span>
         + <span class="t">vec3</span>(<span class="n">1.0</span>)  * fre * <span class="n">0.25</span>                      <span class="c">// fresnel rim</span>
         + <span class="t">vec3</span>(<span class="n">1.0</span>,<span class="n">0.9</span>,<span class="n">0.8</span>) * <span class="f">pow</span>(dif, <span class="n">64.0</span>);          <span class="c">// specular</span>
}
```

